Dear Mike,

	You can't prevent your holy water from disappearing.  It's
automatically used up when you #dip an item.  A cursed item dipped in
holy water becomes uncursed.  An uncursed item dipped in holy water
becomes blessed.  This is nice because one can dip cursed armor and
weapons even, as far as i can tell, after you have readied them. (maybe
it should be called #douse)  Holy water can also be thrown at undead and
demons, and cause damage, but that's a waste of a good remove curse.
	To make holy water, drop a flask of water (a diluted potion) on a
lawful altar.  Water is identified as a clear potion but so is acid. 
Test the clear potion by drinking it (if you have the hp to lose)  or
#dipping an item you don't want (note: i haven't tested this out, but i
imagine an item dipped in acid would dissolve).

	Btw, who in Netland can tell me how to get named weapons?  Do you keep
#offering at your god's altar until you see four leaf clovers and
beyond?  I suppose a wish would work too, or you could find the weapon
on your own.  I found a long sword named Werebane once, that was
identified as +0.  Is that anything special?

